 "drivingQuestion": "Why are both gittin invalid when Hebrew and Greek witnesses alternate?",
 "outcome": "resolved",
 "outcomeNote": "The mishna's ruling is explained against Ze'eiri's dissent.",
 "continuesQuestionOf": "gittin.sugya395",
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "gittin.87b.8",
   "daf": "87b",
   "sentenceId": 7,
   "he": "הָא תָּנֵי זְעֵירִי: שְׁנֵיהֶם כְּשֵׁרִים. וְתַנָּא דִּידַן – דִּלְמָא גּוּנְדָּלִית חֲתֻים; וּתְלָתָא אַחַד, וְחַד אַחַד.",
   "en": "The Gemara answers: «Ze’eiri» in fact «teaches» that «both of them are valid.» The Gemara asks: «And» what is the reasoning of «the tanna of our» mishna? The Gemara answers: He is concerned that «perhaps they signed in reverse,» i.e., perhaps one of the witnesses who signed in Greek reversed the word order of his signature, «and» in actuality he signed the other bill of divorce. Consequently, «three» witnesses signed «one» bill of divorce «and» only «one» witness signed the other «one.» Therefore, they are both rendered invalid."
  }
 ],
